[KiCad-IOS port] Round 22 crash hunt #3/#4/#5: the remaining
desktop-OpenGL canvas constructions outside the footprint
chooser are removed or made fail-safe on iOS.

Diagnosis (hidden_files/round22-bug-ledger.md #3/#4/#5, census
in round22-hunt-crash.md): patch 0051 covers the footprint
chooser. The whole-tree census of raw wxGLCanvas constructions
(EDA_3D_CANVAS / EDA_3D_MODEL_VIEWER — the class of canvas that
bypasses the Cairo forcing at SwitchBackend, patches 0035/
0036) found three more reachable sites, all with the same
hard-fault mechanism on wxQt/iOS (GL context creation cannot
fail cleanly; no desktop OpenGL exists on iOS):

- #3 Footprint Properties (DIALOG_FOOTPRINT_PROPERTIES, opened
  by double-clicking a footprint in the PCB or Footprint
  editor) builds its 3D Models page eagerly, and
  PANEL_PREVIEW_3D_MODEL's constructor creates an EDA_3D_CANVAS
  — so the dialog itself would crash on open.
- #4 DIALOG_SELECT_3D_MODEL (opened from that page to pick a
  model file) creates an EDA_3D_MODEL_VIEWER (a raw
  HIDPI_GL_CANVAS) in its constructor.
- #5 The 3D viewer frame (EDA_3D_VIEWER_FRAME) creates the
  same canvas in its constructor; every entry point (PCB
  editor / footprint viewer / footprint wizard "3D Viewer"
  action, the footprint chooser's external viewer) funnels
  through PCB_BASE_FRAME::CreateAndShow3D_Frame. The 3D viewer
  is a long-standing named limitation of this port — the bug
  is that it fails DEADLY instead of safe.

Fix (all under #ifdef KICAD_IOS_PORT, desktop builds
byte-unchanged):
- panel_preview_3d_model.cpp: skip the canvas (and the
  space-mouse plugin that drives it); the preview pane stays
  empty while the model list and scale/rotation/offset
  controls keep working. Guard the loadSettings() call (it
  asserts on a null canvas), the dispatcher/infobar/sizer
  wiring, the viewer-control tool invocation, and the three
  ReloadRequest/Refresh update sites. Trace:
  "round22-3dpreview-skipped".
- dialog_select_3d_model.cpp: skip the model viewer; the file
  tree and filename controls are unaffected. Guard the
  constructor's Refresh/SetFocus (the other two uses were
  already null-guarded upstream). Trace:
  "round22-3dmodelviewer-skipped".
- pcb_base_frame.cpp: CreateAndShow3D_Frame() on iOS shows
  "The 3D viewer is not available in this port..." and returns
  nullptr instead of constructing the frame. Trace:
  "round22-3dviewer-unavailable".
- Null-guard the two ReparentModal( draw3DFrame ) call sites
  that would otherwise deref the new nullptr return
  (pcb_viewer_tools.cpp Show3DViewer, footprint_chooser_
  frame.cpp Show3DViewerFrame). PCB_BASE_FRAME::Update3DView
  already null-guards upstream.

Gate: hidden_files/round22_gate.py requires the UTF-32LE
literals "round22-3dpreview-skipped", "round22-3dmodelviewer-
skipped" and "round22-3dviewer-unavailable" in the shipped
binaries; the Round 21 IPA must FAIL all three.

Modified files:
  3d-viewer/dialogs/panel_preview_3d_model.cpp
  3d-viewer/dialogs/dialog_select_3d_model.cpp
  pcbnew/pcb_base_frame.cpp
  pcbnew/tools/pcb_viewer_tools.cpp
  pcbnew/footprint_chooser_frame.cpp

